# Line-ending policy for generated files that the build verifies byte-for-byte.
#
# THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. scripts/generate-llms-txt.ts writes these files with
# LF, and its `--check` mode (run in prebuild as verify:llms) does a raw string
# compare of the file on disk against a freshly generated copy. On Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, git rewrites the committed file to CRLF on checkout, so a
# fresh clone has CRLF on disk while the generator emits LF. The compare then
# fails on every line ending and the production build aborts with
# "llms.txt is out of date", even though the content is identical.
#
# Forcing these paths to LF makes the working-tree copy match what the generator
# writes, so the check passes on any platform. git diff and content
# normalization both hide the CRLF/LF split, which is why this took a while to
# see: the only visible diff was the date stamp.
public/llms.txt        text eol=lf
public/llms-full.txt   text eol=lf

# The link manifest is regenerated by links:generate in prebuild and compared by
# audit:links. That check is warn-only so it never failed the build, but pinning
# it to LF keeps a fresh Windows clone from showing it as spuriously modified.
data/internal-links.json text eol=lf
